# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — Appendix E rules 39 & 40, Appendix A (PDF pp. 122, 125, 148).
# A secret pushed once is compromised forever, even if deleted in a later
# commit, because it remains in git history. Rotate in the console instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
credentials.json
token.json
*.credentials.json
*.token.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.secrets/

# Per-peer private config (opponent URLs, group identity) -- copied from the
# *.example templates and edited locally for each match/opponent. Never the
# shared, signed config/game.json, which stays tracked.
config/police/game.toml
config/thief/game.toml
config/*/game.toml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COURSE MATERIAL — do not redistribute.
# The specification PDF is the lecturer's copyrighted work ("all rights
# reserved", Dr. Yoram Segal, 2026). The submission repositories are public, or
# shared outside the course, so committing it would republish it. Everything the
# project needs from it is extracted into docs/ with page references.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
police_thief_p2p.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling / test caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output.
# NOTE: match artefacts (declaration/config/log/result JSON) are DELIBERATELY
# NOT ignored — Appendix F §2 (PDF p. 156) requires each match's config file to
# be committed, and the replay verifier needs the logs. Only scratch output is
# ignored here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
tmp/
*.log
logs/
